      "text": "Before retiring in ‘23, I worked in the nutrition field for 30+ years (and ended my work career in IT)…enjoying food is good - BUT, from a nutrition/health standpoint, I would discourage high calorie/fat intakes per meal AND (discourage) back-to-back meals (which can add even more calories/fat)…\n\nFrom watching Mark, it is my sense that he has a voracious appetite, and while he may still be discerning about food taste/texture/quality, he generally loves food and has a wide range of acceptability food-wise - so unless it tastes “awful”, he will enjoy the foods he eats…I believe Mark and I are similar in food acceptability - treating a meal as a “sensory experience”…",
